    "message": "fix(desktop): stop the tray reverting settings changed elsewhere\n\nToggling one RTK agent from the tray silently reverted whatever the\ndashboard had changed. `_toggle_rtk_agent` flipped one entry in a cache\nsnapshotted at tray construction and then wrote ALL THREE fields\nreconstructed from that stale cache. Enable `codex` in the dashboard,\ntoggle `claude` in the tray, and `codex` goes back off.\n\nMechanism: the tray and the admin HTTP API are separate processes that\nboth persist RtkState to ~/.fcc/rtk.json, with no lock and no\ncross-process notification. The API re-reads fresh state before writing\n(admin_routes.py, `current = await asyncio.to_thread(load_rtk_state)`);\nthe tray did not. The write itself is atomic via os.replace, so this was\na lost update rather than a corrupt file -- the setting simply vanished.\n\n`_toggle_rtk_agent` now re-reads from disk, flips only the requested\nagent on that fresh state, and refreshes the in-memory cache from it so\nthe checkmarks match reality. No locking or IPC: read-modify-write is\nthe whole fix. A comment records why, so it is not \"optimised\" back into\na cached write later.\n\nAlso fixed, same file and same root cause in a smaller form: the\n`Start at Login` and `Tray Enabled` toggles derived their new value from\nthe stale cached field. `config/desktop.py::_update_state` re-reads\nbefore writing, so these could never clobber a *different* field -- but\nthey could compute the wrong direction. If the dashboard turned\n`start_at_login` on after the tray started, the tray's next click wrote\nTrue over True and appeared to do nothing. Both now derive the new value\nfrom persisted state. `_set_server_mode` writes an absolute value and\nwas never affected.\n\nVerification:\n- New lost-update regression test drives the real tray menu items: an\n  external writer enables `codex` after construction, the tray toggles\n  `claude`, and `codex` must survive -- plus the cache must be refreshed.\n- Two new tests for the boolean toggles, asserting an externally changed\n  field toggles in the correct direction.\n- All three proved real by reverting the fix by hand: the RTK test fails\n  with codex False != True, and the two boolean tests fail with\n  assert True is False / assert False is True. Restored and re-passed.\n- tests/cli: 285 passed. ruff format, ruff check, ty check: all clean.\n\nNot done: the tray still holds an in-memory cache rather than reading\nstate per menu render, so checkmarks can display a stale value until the\nnext toggle. Fixing that is a menu-rendering change, not a data-loss\none, and is out of scope here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
